TIP:  Uggh.  The chords are fairly straight forward but Stipe's stilted cadence makes transcribing R.E.M. songs a pain.  But here it is.

TIP:  If tranposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The intro starts with 4 picked notes (notes may or may not transpose).  Untransposed, form (C) and pick the 4th string.  Then lift off the middle finger so the 4th string is now open.  Pick the open 4th string, the 5th string, the open 4th string again, return the middle finger and play chord (C).  And note it repeats again after the first chorus but there's a brief pause to let you come off the (G) to get in position.
  
 
